nd fermented milk on lactose absorption.N'DJITOYAP NDAM C:N'Djitoyap Ndam C is an author who has made significant contributions to the study of yogurt and its effects on lactose absorption. Through their research, N'Djitoyap Ndam C has explored how yogurt can influence the body's ability to absorb lactose, providing valuable insights into dietary practices and health.LAVOINE A:Lavoine A is an author who is actively involved in research concerning yogurt and lactose absorption. This research focuses on the effects of yogurt on lactose absorption, highlighting Lavoine A's contributions to the field.HELLOT MF:Hellot MF is an author who has conducted research on the effects of yogurt in relation to lactase activity and lactose absorption, particularly focusing on individuals who are lactase-deficient. Through their studies, Hellot MF has explored how yogurt consumption may influence the ability to digest lactose, providing insights into dietary management for those with lactose intolerance.ANTOINE JM:Antoine JM is an author who has contributed to research focused on yogurt and lactose absorption. His work in this area highlights the significance of yogurt in relation to lactose digestion and its potential benefits for individuals with lactose intolerance.COLIN R:Colin R is an author known for his contributions to the study of yogurt and its effects on lactose absorption. He has specifically researched how yogurt impacts lactose absorption in individuals who are lactase-deficient, highlighting the potential benefits of yogurt for those with lactose intolerance.JOHN HOPKINS UNIVERSITY:John Hopkins University is a research university located in Baltimore, known for its contributions to various fields including medicine and nutrition.GARCIA-PERIS P:Garcia-Peris P is an author who contributed to the recommendations on nutrition for lactose intolerance.TERRY G. J. DERKS:Terry G. J. Derks is an author who has researched lipids in hepatic glycogen storage disease.MART√çNEZ AUGU