ùªUº;@–äªÏTü<´—Oº≈º~Â	ΩI˜mΩ¡¯è<ÊΩË˙•;ÑsGºËVò;˜‡„ºü‡©;{"title": "HIPOALANINEMIA:"}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE MCARDLE:Enfermedad de McArdle, also known as Glycogen Storage Disease Type V, is a metabolic myopathy caused by a mutation in the muscle isoform of glycogen phosphorylase, leading to exercise intolerance and muscle symptoms."}{"title": "PYGM:PYGM is the gene responsible for encoding the muscle isoform of glycogen phosphorylase, which is mutated in McArdle disease."}{"title": "CK:CK, or creatine kinase, is an enzyme that is typically elevated in individuals with muscle damage, including those with McArdle disease."}{"title": "FOREARM NON-ISQUEMIC TEST:The forearm non-ischemic test is a diagnostic procedure used to measure lactate and ammonia levels in patients suspected of having McArdle disease."}{"title": "CICLOERG\u00d3METRO:A cicloerg\u00f3metro is a device used to measure heart rate and exercise capacity, which can help confirm the second wind phenomenon in McArdle disease patients."}{"title": "BIOPSIA MUSCULAR:Muscle biopsy is a diagnostic procedure that can show focal accumulations of normal glycogen and assess enzyme activity in patients with McArdle disease."}{"title": "EJERCICIO AER\u00d3BICO LIGERO-MODERADO:Light to moderate aerobic exercise is recommended for patients with McArdle disease to improve physical fitness and increase muscle oxidative capacity."}{"title": "GSDVI:Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI) is a rare metabolic disorder characterized by a mutation in the liver isoform of glycogen phosphorylase. This condition is similar to Glycogen Storage Disease Type IX (GSDIX) and necessitates dietary management to address liver-related issues. Individuals with GSDVI often experience symptoms such as hepatomegaly and hypoglycemia, particularly in early childhood."}{"title": "PYGL:The PYGL gene is responsible for encoding the liver isoform of glycogen phosphorylase, which is crucial for glycogenolysis."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN PHOSPHORYLASE:Glycogen phosphorylase is the enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate, playing a key role in glucose metabolism."}{"title": "AMNIOCENTESIS:Amniocentesis is a medical procedure utilized for prenatal diagnosis, allowing for the analysis of amniotic fluid to detect various genetic conditions. This procedure can be employed to identify galactosemia, a metabolic disorder, as well as to detect the mutation associated with Glycogen Storage Disease Type VI (GSDVI). Through the examination of the amniotic fluid, healthcare providers can gain valuable insights into the genetic health of the fetus."}{"title": "GSDIX:GSDIX is a condition that primarily affects the liver and is classified as the most common glycogen storage disease, with an estimated prevalence of 1 in 100,000 individuals. This condition arises from mutations in genes that code for phosphorylase b kinase, which plays a crucial role in glycogen metabolism. To manage the symptoms of GSDIX, particularly hypoglycemia, specific dietary treatments are required."}{"title": "PHKA2:PHKA2 is a gene located on the X chromosome that codes for the hepatic isoform of the alpha subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXa."}{"title": "PHKB:PHKB is a gene located on chromosome 16 that codes for the beta subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXb."}{"title": "PHKG2:PHKG2 is a gene located on chromosome 16 that codes for the gamma subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXc."}{"title": "PHKA1:PHKA1 is a gene located on the X chromosome that codes for the muscular isoform of the alpha subunit of phosphorylase b kinase, associated with glycogen storage disease IXd."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE:Glycogen storage disease refers to a group of inherited metabolic disorders characterized by the abnormal storage of glycogen in the body. These disorders arise from enzyme deficiencies that disrupt the normal metabolism of glycogen, leading to its accumulation in various tissues."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN HC:A diet rich in carbohydrates (HC) is recommended for patients with glycogen storage diseases to manage their condition and prevent hypoglycemia."}{"title": "CROMOSOMA X:Cromosoma X is one of the sex chromosomes in humans, playing a crucial role in genetic inheritance and the determination of biological sex. It is notable for housing several important genes, including those related to glycogen storage diseases. Additionally, the X chromosome contains the gene responsible for X-ALD (X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy), which is specifically located at the Xq28 position. This highlights the significance of Cromosoma X in both normal physiological functions and in the context of certain genetic disorders."}{"title": "CROMOSOMA 16:Chromosome 16, also known as Cromosoma 16, is an autosome in humans that plays a significant role in genetic health. It contains genes associated with various diseases, including mutations linked to inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, this chromosome houses several genes related to glycogen storage diseases, highlighting its importance in metabolic functions and disease susceptibility."}{"title": "AGUACATE:Aguacate is a fruit that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "ALBARICOQUE:Albaricoque is a fruit characterized by its delicate flavor and notable nutritional benefits. It contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 g, and has a fructose content of 0.9 g per 100 g. This combination of low galactose and moderate fructose levels contributes to its appeal as a healthy dietary option."}{"title": "CACAHUETE:Cacahuete is a type of nut that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "CEREZA:Cereza, commonly known as cherry, is a small, round fruit that can be either sweet or sour. It is characterized by its delightful sweet and tart flavor, making it a popular choice for various culinary applications, including desserts, jams, and beverages. Nutritionally, Cereza contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 g, and has a fructose content of 5 g per 100 g. This combination of flavors and nutritional properties contributes to its appeal and versatility in the kitchen."}{"title": "FRESA:Fresa, commonly known as strawberry, is a red, juicy fruit celebrated for its sweetness. It is frequently utilized in a variety of culinary applications, including desserts, salads, and smoothies. Additionally, Fresa is notable for its nutritional profile, containing a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This makes it a suitable option for individuals who need to monitor their galactose intake."}{"title": "LIM\u00d3N:Lim\u00f3n is a fruit that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "MANGO:Mango is a tropical stone fruit recognized for its sweet, juicy flesh. It is commonly used in a variety of culinary applications, including desserts, salads, and smoothies. Additionally, mango contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams, making it a suitable option for those monitoring their galactose intake."}{"title": "POMELO:Pomelo is a large citrus fruit recognized for its refreshing taste. It contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 g, and has a fructose content ranging from 1.5 to 2 g per 100 g."}{"title": "UVA VERDE:Uva verde is a fruit that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "ALCACHOFA:Alcachofa is a vegetable recognized for its nutritional properties, particularly its content of fructans, which may trigger symptoms in individuals with FODMAP intolerance. Additionally, it contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This combination of characteristics makes alcachofa a noteworthy food item for those managing dietary sensitivities."}{"title": "BERENJENA:Berenjena, commonly known as eggplant, is a vegetable recognized for its unique flavor and texture. It is utilized in a variety of cuisines around the world. Additionally, Berenjena contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams, making it a suitable option for those monitoring their galactose intake."}{"title": "CARDO:Cardo is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "COL RIZADA:Col rizada is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "COLIFLOR:Coliflor is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "LECHUGA:Lechuga is a leafy green vegetable known for its dietary fiber content. It is characterized by having a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This makes lechuga a nutritious option for those looking to incorporate healthy greens into their diet."}{"title": "ESP\u00c1RRAGO:Esp\u00e1rrago is a vegetable that is recognized for its nutritional properties. It contains fructans, which may trigger symptoms in individuals who are sensitive to FODMAPs. Additionally, Esp\u00e1rrago has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 grams. This combination of characteristics makes Esp\u00e1rrago a noteworthy food item, particularly for those managing dietary sensitivities."}{"title": "ESPINACA:Espinaca is a vegetable known for its nutritional profile, particularly its low galactose content, which is less than 5 mg per 100 grams."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdA VERDE:Jud\u00eda verde is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "MA\u00cdZ DULCE:Ma\u00edz dulce, also known as sweet corn, is a variety of corn recognized for its sweetness. It is commonly consumed fresh or incorporated into various dishes. This vegetable is notable for its low galactose content, containing less than 5 mg per 100 grams."}{"title": "PEPINO:Pepino is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "R\u00c1BANO:R\u00e1bano is a vegetable that contains a low amount of galactose, less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "REMOLACHA:REMOLACHA, commonly known as beetroot, is a root vegetable recognized for its sweet flavor and vibrant color. It is often utilized in salads and various cooking applications. This vegetable contains high levels of oxalate, which may increase the risk of kidney stone formation. Additionally, REMOLACHA has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "CIRUELA:Ciruela is a fruit recognized for its health benefits and sweet flavor. It contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams. Additionally, Ciruela has a fructose content of 4 grams per 100 grams, contributing to its overall nutritional profile."}{"title": "FRAMBUESA:Frambuesa, commonly known as raspberry, is a small fruit that can be red or black in color. It is celebrated for its sweet and tart flavor, making it a popular choice in various culinary applications, particularly in desserts and jams. In terms of nutritional content, Frambuesa contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams."}{"title": "MELOCOT\u00d3N:Melocot\u00f3n is a fruit commonly known as a peach. It contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams. Additionally, Melocot\u00f3n is a good source of dietary fiber, contributing to its nutritional value."}{"title": "PL\u00c1TANO:Pl\u00e1tano is a type of banana, recognized as a fruit that is rich in dietary fiber. It is a food item that can contain varying levels of FODMAPs, which may impact individuals who are sensitive to these compounds. Additionally, Pl\u00e1tano contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams."}{"title": "COL DE BRUSELAS:Col de Bruselas is a vegetable that contains a moderate amount of galactose, between 5-10 mg per 100 g."}{"title": "D\u00c1TIL:D\u00e1til, also known as date, is a sweet fruit commonly found in Middle Eastern cuisine. It is often consumed dried or used in various desserts. In terms of nutritional content, D\u00e1til contains a higher amount of galactose, ranging from 10 to 20 mg per 100 grams. This fruit is not only a popular ingredient in culinary dishes but also offers specific nutritional benefits."}{"title": "GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA:Galactosa-1-fosfato uridil transferasa (GALT) is an enzyme that converts galactose-1-phosphate and uridine diphosphate glucose into uridine diphosphate galactose and glucose-1-phosphate, and is expressed by the GALT gene on chromosome 9p13."}{"title": "GALACTITOL:Galactitol is a sugar alcohol that is produced from galactose through the action of aldose reductase. It is a metabolite that can accumulate in the lens of the eye, particularly in patients with galactosemia, a metabolic disorder characterized by the inability to properly metabolize galactose. This accumulation of galactitol is associated with the development of cataracts, a common complication in individuals with classic galactosemia and those with galactokinase deficiency. In patients with galactosemia, monitoring the levels of galactitol is important to assess dietary compliance and potential transgressions, as elevated levels can indicate toxicity and contribute to the risk of cataract formation."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO GALACT\u00d3NICO:\u00c1cido galact\u00f3nico is a metabolite that is formed from galactose and plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It is produced through the action of the enzyme galactose dehydrogenase and can be utilized in alternative metabolic pathways. This compound is integral to the overall process of galactose metabolization, highlighting its importance in biochemical processes related to this sugar."}{"title": "V\u00cdA LELOIR:The Leloir pathway is a metabolic pathway that converts galactose into glucose, involving several enzymatic steps and is crucial for proper carbohydrate metabolism."}{"title": "GEN GALT:The GALT gene is responsible for encoding the enzyme galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase, and mutations in this gene can lead to galactosemia."}{"title": "GALACTOSA DESHIDROGENASA:Galactosa deshidrogenasa, also known as galactose dehydrogenase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It catalyzes the oxidation of galactose, converting it into \u00e1cido galact\u00f3nico (galactonic acid). This enzymatic reaction is an important step in the metabolic pathway of galactose, facilitating its proper utilization in biological processes."}{"title": "ALDOSA REDUCTASA:Aldose reductase is an enzyme that converts galactose into galactitol, playing a role in the polyol pathway of sugar metabolism."}{"title": "GALACTOKINASA:Galactokinasa, also known as galactokinase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It catalyzes the conversion of galactose into galactose-1-phosphate (Gal-1-P), which is the first step in the metabolic pathway for galactose. This enzyme is particularly significant in the context of the genetic condition known as galactosemia, a disorder that affects the body's ability to process galactose properly. The activity of galactokinasa is essential for the proper metabolism of galactose, and deficiencies in this enzyme can lead to the accumulation of galactose in the body, resulting in various health complications associated with galactosemia."}{"title": "FISIOPATOL\u00d3GIA Y DIAGN\u00d3STICO:The section on physiopathology and diagnosis discusses the clinical implications and diagnostic criteria for galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase deficiency or galactosemia."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO URIDIL TRANSFERASA:Galactose-1-phosphate uridil transferase deficiency, also known as galactosemia, is a genetic disorder that affects the metabolism of galactose."}{"title": "GLUCOPROTE\u00cdNAS Y GLUCOL\u00cdPIDOS:Glycoproteins and glycolipids are biomolecules formed from carbohydrates and play essential roles in cell structure and function."}{"title": "LACTASA:LACTASA is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the digestion of lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. It hydrolyzes lactose into its constituent sugars, glucose and galactose, which are essential for energy derived from milk carbohydrates in mammals. A deficiency in lactase is commonly observed in patients with celiac disease, leading to lactose intolerance. Although lactase is not inducible, its production can adapt with continuous consumption of lactose, allowing some individuals to better digest lactose over time."}{"title": "GALACTOSEMIA CL\u00c1SICA:Galactosemia cl\u00e1sica es una enfermedad metab\u00f3lica causada por un d\u00e9ficit grave de la actividad enzim\u00e1tica, con una incidencia de 1:50,000 reci\u00e9n nacidos vivos y manifestaciones cl\u00ednicas que comienzan tras el nacimiento."}{"title": "GALT:GALT, or Galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase, is a crucial enzyme responsible for the metabolism of galactose. The gene GALT is essential for this process, and mutations in this gene lead to a condition known as classical galactosemia. The activity of the GALT enzyme is measured to diagnose galactosemia and its various forms. This enzyme plays a significant role in the proper processing of galactose, and its deficiency can result in serious metabolic complications."}{"title": "ERITROCITOS:Erythrocytes, also known as red blood cells, play a significant role in the diagnosis of galactosemia by measuring GALT activity and galactose levels. These cells express the galactokinase gene (GALK1), which is crucial for galactose metabolism. Additionally, erythrocytes exhibit enzymatic activity related to galactose, further highlighting their importance in metabolic processes involving this sugar."}{"title": "NORTE DE EUROPA:Regi\u00f3n donde se encuentra la mutaci\u00f3n homocigota cl\u00e1sica del gen GALT, t\u00edpica en la poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "SUR DE ALEMANIA:Regi\u00f3n donde se encuentra una mutaci\u00f3n relativamente frecuente del gen GALT que causa galactosemia cl\u00e1sica."}{"title": "CROACIA:Pa\u00eds donde se encuentra una mutaci\u00f3n del gen GALT que causa galactosemia cl\u00e1sica."}{"title": "CRISTALINO:El cristalino es una parte del ojo donde se depositan los efectos osm\u00f3ticos del galactitol en pacientes con galactosemia cl\u00e1sica."}{"title": "NIVEL DE GALACTOSA:Los niveles de galactosa libre plasm\u00e1tica son un indicador clave en el diagn\u00f3stico de galactosemia cl\u00e1sica."}{"title": "NIVEL DE GAL-1-P:NIVEL DE GAL-1-P is a significant marker in the diagnosis and management of classic galactosemia. The levels of Gal-1-P in erythrocytes serve as an important indicator for diagnosing this condition. Additionally, monitoring the level of Gal-1-P is crucial for assessing the effectiveness of dietary restrictions in individuals affected by galactosemia."}{"title": "DIAGN\u00d3STICO:The entity \"DIAGN\u00d3STICO\" encompasses various processes related to the identification of medical conditions and diseases. Diagnosis of fructan intolerance typically involves dietary elimination and monitoring symptom improvement. In the context of inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosis is essential for effective management. Additionally, \"diagn\u00f3stico\" refers to identifying elevated homocysteine levels, which is often done through plasma concentration tests. It also includes the identification of urea cycle disorders through biochemical tests and enzyme activity measurements. In the realm of food allergies and intolerances, diagnosis involves pinpointing the cause of symptoms through testing and ruling out other disorders. Furthermore, early diagnosis of classic galactosemia is critical to prevent complications. Overall, \"DIAGN\u00d3STICO\" represents a comprehensive approach to identifying various health conditions through specific testing and assessment methods."}{"title": "\u0392-CETOGALACT\u00d3NICO:\u03b2-Cetogalact\u00f3nico es un metabolito en la v\u00eda de metabolizaci\u00f3n de la galactosa."}{"title": "XILULOSA:Xilulosa es un metabolito que se forma en la v\u00eda de las pentosas fosfato, relacionada con el metabolismo de la galactosa."}{"title": "V\u00cdA DE LAS PENTOSAS FOSFATO:La v\u00eda de las pentosas fosfato es una ruta metab\u00f3lica que genera intermediarios importantes en el metabolismo de carbohidratos, incluyendo galactosa."}{"title": "GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO:Galactosa-1-fosfato es un metabolito que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es crucial para su conversi\u00f3n a glucosa."}{"title": "UDP-GALACTOSA:UDP-galactosa es un nucle\u00f3tido que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es importante para la s\u00edntesis de macromol\u00e9culas glicosiladas."}{"title": "PIRUVATO:Piruvato, also known as pyruvate, is a final metabolite in the glycolysis process, generated from glucose. It is also associated with the metabolism of galactose. Additionally, pyruvate is recognized for its potential benefits in enhancing energy production, particularly among athletes who may utilize it to improve their performance."}{"title": "MACROMOL\u00c9CULAS GLICOSILADAS:Las macromol\u00e9culas glicosiladas son compuestos que se forman a partir de la uni\u00f3n de az\u00facares, incluyendo galactosa, y son importantes en la biolog\u00eda celular."}{"title": "GALACTOL\u00cdPIDOS:Galactol\u00edpidos are lipids that contain galactose, playing a significant role in the context of metabolic disorders associated with galactose. Additionally, they are essential components of cellular membranes, highlighting their importance in both metabolic processes and structural integrity within cells."}{"title": "GALACTOPROTE\u00cdNAS:Las galactoprote\u00ednas son prote\u00ednas que contienen galactosa y desempe\u00f1an roles importantes en diversas funciones biol\u00f3gicas.) <|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "AFROAMERICANS:Afroamericans are a demographic group that is frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, which is associated with a specific genetic mutation."}{"title": "AFRICANS:Africans, particularly those native to South Africa, are also frequently affected by the most common clinical variant of galactosemia, sharing the same genetic mutation as Afroamericans."}{"title": "DUARTE VARIANT:The Duarte variant is a biochemical variant of galactosemia characterized by partial residual GALT activity, leading to milder symptoms and complications compared to classical galactosemia."}{"title": "NEONATAL SCREENING:Neonatal screening for galactosemia is a program that detects elevated levels of galactose and GALT enzyme activity in newborns to diagnose the disorder early."}{"title": "AL\u00c9LO DUARTE:The Duarte allele is a genetic variant associated with a milder form of galactosemia, affecting GALT activity in individuals."}{"title": "NEONATO:A neonate is a newborn baby, particularly one that is suspected to have galactosemia based on screening results or family history."}{"title": "BIOPSIA CORIAL:Chorionic villus sampling (biopsia corial) is a prenatal test that can be used to diagnose genetic disorders, including galactosemia."}{"title": "GAL-1-P:Gal-1-P, also known as Galactose-1-phosphate, is a significant metabolite measured in patients to monitor dietary compliance and metabolic control in individuals with galactosemia. This substance is particularly elevated in patients with certain forms of galactosemia, making it a crucial marker in the screening and management of the disorder."}{"title": "NIVEL DE GALACTITOL:The level of galactitol is monitored in patients with galactosemia to assess dietary compliance and potential complications."}{"title": "FORMULAS DE SOJA:Soy formulas are recommended for infants with galactosemia as a substitute for milk-based formulas."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS:The entity \"ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS\" refers to a category of foods that are permissible for consumption by individuals with specific dietary restrictions. These allowed foods are tailored for patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption, adhering to established dietary guidelines. Additionally, for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, the permitted foods include natural dairy products, certain meats, and specific vegetables. Furthermore, for those with galactosemia, the allowed foods must contain less than 5 mg of galactose per 100 g. Lastly, \"ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS\" also encompasses foods suitable for a broad low-sodium diet, as detailed in Tabla 2. This comprehensive overview highlights the diverse dietary needs that \"ALIMENTOS PERMITIDOS\" addresses, ensuring safe and appropriate food choices for individuals with these conditions."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS PROHIBIDOS:Foods that are prohibited for individuals with galactosemia, which contain more than 20 mg of galactose per 100 g."}{"title": "VISCERAS:Viscera are non-dairy foods that may contain galactose and should be consumed with caution by individuals with galactosemia."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS MANUFACTURADOS:Manufactured foods may contain galactose or lactose and should be carefully checked by individuals with galactosemia."}{"title": "GALK1:GALK1 is the gene that encodes the enzyme galactokinase, located on chromosome 17q25.1."}{"title": "GALE:GALE is a gene located on chromosome 1p36 that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of galactose. It encodes an enzyme known as uridin difosfato galactosa-4-epimerasa (GALE), which is essential for the proper processing of galactose in the body. Mutations or deficiencies in the GALE gene can lead to various clinical deficits, highlighting its importance in metabolic pathways related to galactose."}{"title": "GALACTONATO:Galactonate is a compound derived from galactose that can be used for energy production."}{"title": "CATARATAS:Cataracts are a condition that can develop due to the accumulation of galactitol in the lens of the eye, particularly in infants with galactokinase deficiency."}{"title": "DIETA SIN L\u00c1CTEOS:A lifelong dairy-free diet is recommended for patients with galactokinase deficiency to prevent the formation of cataracts."}{"title": "LEUCOCITOS:Leucocitos, also known as leukocytes, are white blood cells that play a crucial role in the immune response. They are involved in defending the body against infections and diseases. Additionally, leucocitos are affected by galactose metabolism, as they express the galactokinase gene (GALK1), which is essential for the metabolism of galactose. This connection highlights the dual role of leucocitos in both immune function and metabolic processes."}{"title": "ALDOB:ALDOB is a gene located on chromosome 9q22.3 that encodes the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase. This enzyme plays a crucial role in fructose metabolism. Additionally, ALDOB is significant in the context of hereditary fructose intolerance, as it is the gene responsible for encoding the enzyme that is deficient in this condition."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT PERIF\u00c9RICO:D\u00e9ficit perif\u00e9rico is a clinical form of galactosemia limited to erythrocytes and leukocytes, resulting in asymptomatic individuals."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT GENERALIZADO:D\u00e9ficit generalizado is a clinical form of galactosemia where GALE activity is deficient in all tissues, resembling classic galactosemia."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT INTERMEDIO:D\u00e9ficit intermedio is a clinical form of galactosemia with reduced GALE activity in erythrocytes and leukocytes, but not presenting acute symptoms at birth."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA-1-FOSFATO:Fructose-1-phosphate is a compound that accumulates in the body due to the deficiency of the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA-6-FOSFATO:Fructose-6-phosphate is an intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is affected by fructose metabolism."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA-1,6 BIFOSFATO:Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate is a key intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is produced from fructose-1-phosphate."}{"title": "GLICERALDEHIDO:Glyceraldehyde is a product of fructose metabolism that is involved in energy production."}{"title": "GLICERALDEHIDO-3-FOSFATO:Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is an important intermediate in the glycolytic pathway derived from glyceraldehyde."}{"title": "DIHIDROXIACETONA FOSFATO:Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is another product of fructose metabolism that plays a role in energy production."}{"title": "MUSCULO Y OTROS TEJIDOS:Muscle and other tissues are involved in the metabolism of fructose and its intermediates."}{"title": "HEREDITARY FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE:Hereditary fructose intolerance is a genetic condition that impairs the body's ability to metabolize fructose. This metabolic disorder can lead to a range of clinical manifestations, particularly complicating dietary management in infants. Individuals with this condition are unable to properly process fructose, which can result in various health issues."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA-1-FOSFATO ALDOLASA:Fructosa-1-fosfato aldolasa is an enzyme involved in the metabolism of fructose, and its deficiency leads to hereditary fructose intolerance."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS NO PERMITIDOS:\"ALIMENTOS NO PERMITIDOS\" refers to foods that must be avoided by individuals with specific dietary restrictions. These prohibited foods include items that should be excluded from the diets of patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption, as outlined in dietary guidelines. Additionally, for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, prohibited foods encompass condensed milk, industrial ice creams, and certain processed meats. It is essential for those affected by these conditions to adhere to these restrictions to manage their health effectively."}{"title": "FOLATO:FOLATO is a B vitamin that plays a vital role in cell division, DNA synthesis, and repair. It is particularly crucial during periods of rapid growth, making it essential for various life stages. Dietary intake recommendations for folate emphasize its importance in maintaining overall health. Additionally, folate is recommended as a vitamin supplement for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, highlighting its significance in supporting health in specific populations."}{"title": "COMPLEJO B:COMPLEJO B refers to a group of B-complex vitamins that play a crucial role in health and metabolic processes. These vitamins are often found to be deficient in cirrhotic patients, which can negatively impact their overall health and recovery. Additionally, Vitamin B complex is recommended for individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance, as it supports essential metabolic functions. Thus, COMPLEJO B is significant for both individuals with liver conditions and those with specific metabolic disorders."}{"title": "BRUSELAS:Bruselas is a city known for its diverse agricultural products including various vegetables and fruits."}{"title": "MANDARINA:Mandarina is a small citrus fruit known for its sweet and tangy flavor, making it a popular choice among fruit lovers. It has a fructose content of 2.8 g per 100 g, contributing to its delightful taste. Additionally, Mandarina is recognized for its dietary fiber content, which adds to its nutritional benefits."}{"title": "LIMON:Lim\u00f3n is a citrus fruit with a low fructose content of 0.6 g/100 g, commonly used for flavoring and beverages."}{"title": "LIMA:Lima is a citrus fruit with a fructose content of 0.5 g/100 g, often used in cooking and drinks."}{"title": "UVA:UVA, or grape, is a type of fruit that is recognized for its high fructose content, ranging from 8.1 to 10.5 grams per 100 grams. It is commonly utilized in winemaking and as a snack. Additionally, grapes are recommended as part of a hypocaloric diet, highlighting their nutritional value and versatility in various dietary plans."}{"title": "MELON:Mel\u00f3n is a fruit with a fructose content of 2-4 g/100 g, popular for its refreshing taste in summer."}{"title": "SANDIA:Sand\u00eda is a fruit with a fructose content of 3 g/100 g, widely enjoyed for its hydrating properties."}{"title": "MARACUYA:Maracuy\u00e1 is a fruit with a fructose content of 1.9 g/100 g, appreciated for its exotic flavor."}{"title": "GRANADA:Granada is a fruit characterized by its tough outer skin and numerous seeds. It has a fructose content of 5.7 g per 100 g and is recognized for its sweet and tart flavor. Additionally, Granada is noted for its antioxidant properties, making it a popular choice in cooking and garnishing."}{"title": "CEBOLLETA:Cebollita is a type of green onion that is often used as a garnish or in salads."}{"title": "BATATA:Batata, also known as sweet potato, is a starchy root vegetable that is rich in vitamins."}{"title": "MAIZ DULCE:Ma\u00edz dulce is a variety of corn that is sweet and often eaten as a vegetable."}{"title": "CHIRIVIA:Chiriv\u00eda is a root vegetable similar to parsnip, known for its sweet flavor."}{"title": "JUDIAS VERDES:Jud\u00edas verdes are green beans that are commonly used in salads and as a side dish."}{"title": "PIMIENTOS:Pimientos are peppers that come in various colors and are used for their flavor and color in dishes."}{"title": "VERDURAS PROCESADAS ENLATADAS:Verduras procesadas enlatadas are canned vegetables that are often used for convenience in cooking."}{"title": "SOPAS:SOPAS are liquid dishes commonly known as soups, typically prepared by boiling a variety of ingredients, including meat, vegetables, or grains. These dishes may also incorporate lactose-containing ingredients, adding to their flavor and texture."}{"title": "CALDOS:Caldos are broths made from simmering meat, vegetables, or fish, used as a base for soups and sauces."}{"title": "CONDIMENTOS:Condimentos are substances used to enhance the flavor of food, including spices and sauces.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MARACUY\u00c1:Maracuy\u00e1, also known as passion fruit, is a tropical fruit with a tough outer rind and juicy, seed-filled interior, often used in beverages and desserts."}{"title": "MORA:Mora, or blackberry, is a dark purple fruit that is sweet and tart, often used in jams, desserts, and smoothies."}{"title": "AR\u00c1NDANO:Ar\u00e1ndano, or blueberry, is a small, round fruit that is sweet and often used in desserts, smoothies, and as a health food."}{"title": "PAPAYA:Papaya is a tropical fruit with orange flesh and black seeds, known for its sweet flavor and digestive health benefits."}{"title": "PI\u00d1A TROPICAL:Pi\u00f1a tropical, or pineapple, is a tropical fruit with a sweet and tangy flavor, often used in desserts, drinks, and savory dishes."}{"title": "COCO:Coco, commonly known as coconut, is a tropical fruit characterized by its hard shell and sweet, creamy flesh. It is widely utilized in various culinary applications, including cooking and beverages, and is recognized for its numerous health benefits."}{"title": "HIGO:Higo, or fig, is a sweet fruit with a unique texture, often eaten fresh or dried and used in desserts and salads."}{"title": "UVA PASA:Uva pasa, or raisin, is a dried grape known for its sweetness, often used in baking and cooking."}{"title": "HIGO SECO:Higo seco, or dried fig, is a sweet, chewy fruit often used in baking and as a snack."}{"title": "CIRUELA PASA:Ciruela pasa, or dried plum, is a sweet, chewy fruit known for its digestive health benefits."}{"title": "ZUMO DE MANZANA:Zumo de manzana, or apple juice, is a beverage made from pressed apples, known for its sweet flavor."}{"title": "ZUMO DE PERA:Zumo de pera, or pear juice, is a beverage made from pressed pears, known for its sweet and mild flavor."}{"title": "ZUMO DE NARANJA:ZUMO DE NARANJA, or orange juice, is a beverage made from pressed oranges, celebrated for its refreshing taste. It is also recommended in a moderate low-sodium diet, highlighting its nutritional benefits and versatility as a healthy drink option."}{"title": "ZUMO DE UVA:Zumo de uva, or grape juice, is a beverage made from pressed grapes, known for its sweet flavor."}{"title": "TEMA 14:Tema 14 discusses nutritional support in pathologies with alterations in processing, focusing on dietary considerations and food choices."}{"title": "PI\u00d1A EN ALM\u00cdBAR:Pi\u00f1a en alm\u00edbar is pineapple preserved in syrup, commonly used in desserts and fruit salads."}{"title": "PIMIENTO ROJO:Pimiento rojo, or red bell pepper, is a sweet pepper used in salads, cooking, and as a garnish."}{"title": "DULCE DE MEMBRILLO:Dulce de membrillo is a sweet paste made from quince, a fruit known for its unique flavor. This delicacy is often utilized in desserts and can also be enjoyed as a spread. Additionally, dulce de membrillo is recognized as a permissible item in modified diets, specifically categorized within the sweets and desserts group."}{"title": "REFRESCO:Refresco, or soft drink, is a sweetened beverage, often carbonated, consumed for refreshment."}{"title": "MERMELADA \u00abSIN AZ\u00daCAR\u00bb:Mermelada \u00absin az\u00facar\u00bb is a type of jam made without added sugar, often used as a spread."}{"title": "CHOCOLATE NEGRO:Chocolate negro, also known as dark chocolate, is a type of chocolate characterized by its high cocoa content, which contributes to its rich flavor. It typically contains a higher percentage of cocoa compared to other types of chocolate, making it a popular choice among those seeking a more intense chocolate experience. Additionally, dark chocolate is often regarded as a healthier option due to its higher cocoa content, which is associated with various health benefits."}{"title": "CHOCOLATE CON LECHE:Chocolate con leche, or milk chocolate, is a sweet chocolate made with milk, known for its creamy texture."}{"title": "CHOCOLATE BLANCO:Chocolate blanco, also known as white chocolate, is a type of chocolate made primarily from cocoa butter, sugar, and milk solids. It is characterized by its sweet flavor, which distinguishes it from darker varieties of chocolate that contain cocoa solids. However, it is important to note that white chocolate may contain ingredients that individuals with certain dietary restrictions need to avoid, making it essential for consumers to check the ingredient list before consumption."}{"title": "CHOCOLATE \u00abSIN AZ\u00daCAR\u00bb:Chocolate \u00absin az\u00facar\u00bb is a type of chocolate made without added sugar, often used for dietary purposes."}{"title": "TURR\u00d3N \u00abSIN AZ\u00daCAR\u00bb:Turr\u00f3n \u00absin az\u00facar\u00bb is a type of nougat made without added sugar, often consumed as a sweet treat."}{"title": "GALLETAS \u00abSIN AZ\u00daCAR\u00bb:Galletas \u00absin az\u00facar\u00bb are cookies made without added sugar, often used for dietary purposes."}{"title": "CHICLE \u00abSIN AZ\u00daCAR\u00bb:Chicle \u00absin az\u00facar\u00bb is sugar-free chewing gum, often used as a breath freshener."}{"title": "LIVER:The liver is a vital organ that plays a significant role in various physiological processes. It is primarily affected by hemochromatosis, a condition that can lead to serious complications such as cirrhosis and hepatocarcinoma. Additionally, the liver is the primary site for gluconeogenesis, which is essential for glucose metabolism. This organ's functions are critical for maintaining overall metabolic homeostasis in the body."}{"title": "BRAIN:The brain is a vital organ that relies exclusively on glucose as its energy source."}{"title": "INTESTINE:The intestine is a crucial component of the digestive system, playing a significant role in the absorption of nutrients, which is essential for overall nutrition. Additionally, the intestine is involved in gluconeogenesis, contributing to the production of glucose in the body. However, it is important to note that the intestine can also be a site of inflammation and damage in individuals with celiac disease, where gluten triggers adverse reactions. Thus, the health of the intestine is vital not only for nutrient absorption and glucose production but also for preventing inflammatory conditions related to dietary components."}{"title": "FRUCTOSE-1,6-BISPHOSPHATASE:Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase is an enzyme that is a key regulatory step in gluconeogenesis, converting fructose-1,6-bisphosphate to fructose-6-phosphate."}{"title": "PYRUVATE CARBOXYLASE:Pyruvate carboxylase is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of pyruvate to oxaloacetate, an important step in gluconeogenesis."}{"title": "GLYCERALDEHYDE-3-PHOSPHATE:Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is a three-carbon sugar that is an intermediate in both glycolysis and gluconeogenesis."}{"title": "LACTATE:Lactate is a byproduct of anaerobic metabolism and can be converted back to glucose through gluconeogenesis."}{"title": "FRUCTOSA-1,6-BIFOSFATASA:Fructosa-1,6-bifosfatasa is a key enzyme in gluconeogenesis that catalyzes the conversion of fructose-1,6-bisphosphate to fructose-6-phosphate, and its deficiency leads to a specific metabolic disorder."}{"title": "ACETIL-COA:Acetyl-CoA is a central metabolite in energy production, formed from pyruvate, and plays a crucial role in the Krebs cycle. It serves as a key metabolic intermediate involved in various biochemical pathways, including those affected by Maple Syrup Urine Disease (MSUD)."}{"title": "OXALACETATO:Oxaloacetate is a four-carbon molecule that is a key intermediate in the Krebs cycle and gluconeogenesis, formed from pyruvate."}{"title": "FOSFOENOLPIRUVATO:Phosphoenolpyruvate is an important intermediate in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, derived from oxaloacetate."}{"title": "ASPARTATO:Aspartate, also known as aspartic acid, is an amino acid that can be synthesized from oxaloacetate. It plays a significant role in various metabolic processes, including the urea cycle and gluconeogenesis. Additionally, aspartate is recognized for its benefits in enhancing recovery after exercise, making it a valuable compound for athletes and individuals engaged in physical training."}{"title": "MALATO:Malate is an intermediate in the citric acid cycle and gluconeogenesis, formed from oxaloacetate."}{"title": "GLICEROL-3-FOSFATO:Glycerol-3-phosphate is an intermediate in the conversion of glycerol to glucose and is involved in lipid metabolism."}{"title": "DIHIDROXIACETONA-FOSFATO:Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is an intermediate in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, derived from glycerol-3-phosphate."}{"title": "CICLO DE KREBS:The Krebs cycle, also known as the citric acid cycle, is a key metabolic pathway that generates energy through the oxidation of acetyl-CoA."}{"title": "AMILASA:Amilasa is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of starch into sugars, playing a crucial role in carbohydrate digestion."}{"title": "ALMIDON:Almidon is a polysaccharide that serves as a major carbohydrate storage form in plants, composed of amylose and amylopectin."}{"title": "ISOMALTOSA:Isomaltosa is a disaccharide composed of two glucose units, which is produced during the digestion of starch. It plays a significant role in the digestion and absorption of carbohydrates, particularly through enzymatic reactions."}{"title": "MALTOSA:Maltosa is a disaccharide composed of two glucose molecules, which is formed during the digestion of starch by the enzyme amylase. It plays a significant role in carbohydrate metabolism, highlighting its importance in the body's energy processes."}{"title": "FRUCTANOS:Fructanos are carbohydrates composed of fructose units, functioning as storage carbohydrates in plants and synthesized by certain fungi and bacteria. These naturally occurring carbohydrates are commonly found in cereals and vegetables. However, it is important to note that fructans can lead to intolerance in some individuals when consumed in large quantities."}{"title": "SGLT1:SGLT1 is a sodium-glucose cotransporter that plays a crucial role in the absorption of glucose and galactose in the intestines. It is specifically the intestinal monosaccharide transporter that is influenced by mutations in the SLC5A1 gene. These mutations can result in a condition known as glucose-galactose malabsorption, which impairs the body's ability to absorb these essential sugars."}{"title": "GLUT5:GLUT5 is a transporter protein that facilitates the absorption of fructose in the intestines."}{"title": "ENTEROCITOS:Enterocytes are specialized cells lining the intestines that are involved in nutrient absorption."}{"title": "VENA PORTA:The portal vein is a major vein that carries blood from the gastrointestinal tract to the liver for processing."}{"title": "OLIGOFRACTOSA:Oligofructosa are short-chain fructans recognized for their role as dietary fibers, offering a range of health benefits. This type of prebiotic fiber is particularly noted for its ability to support gut health and is commonly utilized in various dietary formulations."}{"title": "MALTODEXTRINAS:Maltodextrins are carbohydrate polymers and polysaccharides that serve multiple purposes in the food and beverage industry. They are primarily used as food additives and are produced from starch through a process of partial hydrolysis. In sports drinks, maltodextrins play a crucial role by providing energy and enhancing the absorption of fluids. Additionally, they are significant in the digestion process, contributing to the overall nutritional value of various products."}{"title": "SACARASA-ISOMALTASA:Sacarasa-Isomaltasa is an enzyme that plays a vital role in carbohydrate metabolism by breaking down sugars, particularly sucrose and isomaltose. It catalyzes the hydrolysis of sucrose and products derived from starch digestion, such as isomaltose and various dextrins, specifically targeting their \u03b1-1,6 bonds. This enzymatic activity is essential for aiding in digestion and facilitating the proper utilization of carbohydrates in the body."}{"title": "BORDE:Borde refers to the brush border of the intestinal epithelium, where nutrient absorption occurs."}{"title": "CITOPLASMA:Citoplasma is the gel-like substance within cells where various cellular processes occur, including metabolism."}{"title": "TREHALOSA:Trehalosa is a sugar composed of two glucose molecules, known for its role in energy storage and metabolism."}{"title": "POLIOLES:Polioles are sugar alcohols used as sweeteners and are involved in carbohydrate metabolism."}{"title": "MANITOL:Mannitol is a type of polyol, specifically a sugar alcohol, that is commonly used as a sweetener. It possesses unique absorption characteristics in the intestine, which can be beneficial in certain applications. However, it is important to note that mannitol may cause digestive issues for some individuals, highlighting the need for caution in its consumption."}{"title": "MALTITOL:Maltitol is a sugar alcohol used as a sugar substitute, known for its lower caloric content."}{"title": "XILITOL:Xilitol is a sugar alcohol commonly used as a sweetener. It is known for its dental health benefits, making it a popular choice in products aimed at promoting oral hygiene. However, it is important to note that xylitol may cause digestive discomfort in some individuals, particularly when consumed in larger quantities."}{"title": "FOS:FOS, or Fructooligosaccharides, are short-chain fructans that serve as prebiotic fibers, promoting gut health. They are commonly utilized in various dietary products due to their beneficial effects on the digestive system. FOS are recognized for their ability to enhance the growth of beneficial gut bacteria, thereby contributing to overall digestive wellness."}{"title": "GOS:GOS (Galactooligosaccharides) are short-chain galactose polymers that are not digested in the intestine and have prebiotic properties."}{"title": "AGCC:AGCC, or short-chain fatty acids, are produced during the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates and sugars in the colon. These fatty acids play a significant role in gut health by contributing to the maintenance of a healthy gut microbiome. Additionally, AGCC are involved in the reabsorption of water and sodium in the colon, highlighting their importance in overall digestive health and fluid balance."}{"title": "DIGESTI\u00d3N:Digesti\u00f3n is the process of breaking down food into nutrients that can be absorbed by the body."}{"title": "ABSORCI\u00d3N:Absorci\u00f3n is the process by which nutrients from digested food are taken up into the bloodstream."}{"title": "ENZIMAS:Enzymas are biological catalysts that play a crucial role in facilitating biochemical reactions within the body. They are primarily proteins that catalyze chemical reactions, including the digestion of carbohydrates and fats. Enzymas are present in various bodily fluids, such as chyle, where they assist in the digestion of nutrients, ensuring efficient metabolic processes."}{"title": "\u0392-HIDROLASAS:\u03b2-hidrolasas are enzymes that hydrolyze \u03b2-glycosidic bonds in carbohydrates, playing a key role in their digestion."}{"title": "FLORA BACTERIANA:FLORA BACTERIANA refers to the community of bacteria present in the gut, which plays a vital role in the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates. This intestinal flora is unique to each individual and is essential for maintaining digestive health."}{"title": "DISTENSI\u00d3N:Distensi\u00f3n is a condition characterized by swelling or bloating in the abdomen, which can result from the accumulation of gas or fluid. This condition may also arise specifically from the buildup of undigested carbohydrates in the digestive system."}{"title": "MALDIGESTI\u00d3N:Maldigesti\u00f3n is the inadequate digestion of food, which can lead to symptoms such as bloating and discomfort."}{"title": "MICROFLORA COL\u00d3NICA:Microflora col\u00f3nica refers to the bacteria present in the colon that play a crucial role in the fermentation of undigested sugars."}{"title": "TEST DEL ALIENTO:The \"Test del Aliento\" is a diagnostic procedure designed to identify carbohydrate malabsorption, specifically focusing on malabsorption of fructose. This test measures the levels of hydrogen and methane in the breath after the ingestion of fructose. By analyzing these gas levels, healthcare professionals can confirm the presence of fructose malabsorption in patients."}{"title": "ACUMULACI\u00d3N INTRALUMINAL DE AZ\u00daCAR NO DIGERIDO:Accumulation of undigested sugar in the intestinal lumen can lead to symptoms of distension and diarrhea."}{"title": "IRRITACI\u00d3N REGI\u00d3N ANAL Y PERIN\u00c9:Irritation in the anal and perineal region can occur due to the acidic nature of the stool resulting from malabsorption."}{"title": "HIDR\u00d3GENO:Hydrogen is a gas produced during the fermentation of carbohydrates in the colon, which is measured in breath tests for diagnosing malabsorption."}{"title": "METANO:Methane is another gas produced during fermentation in the colon, which can also be measured in breath tests."}{"title": "PREPARACIONES PARA COLONOSCOPIA:Preparaciones para colonoscopia are procedures that can affect the microbiota and should be avoided before breath tests."}{"title": "DIETA BAJA EN HC FERMENTABLES:Dieta baja en HC fermentables is a dietary approach recommended before breath tests to ensure accurate results."}{"title": "LCT:Long-chain triglycerides (LCT) are fats that play a crucial role in providing essential fatty acids, particularly in infant nutrition. However, they may also have adverse effects on liver function in patients suffering from chronic pancreatitis. Additionally, the LCT gene is significant as it encodes the lactase enzyme, which is essential for the digestion of lactose. This gene is responsible for the production of lactase, enabling the breakdown of lactose in the body. Thus, LCT encompasses both dietary fats important for nutrition and a gene vital for lactose metabolism."}{"title": "AFRICA:Africa has a high prevalence of lactose intolerance, ranging from 65-75%."}{"title": "ASIA:Asia has the highest prevalence of lactose intolerance, exceeding 90%."}{"title": "NATIVE AMERICANS:Native Americans have a very high prevalence of lactose intolerance, estimated at 90-95%."}{"title": "HAPLOTYPES:Haplotypes are genetic variations associated with lactase persistence in different populations."}{"title": "SNP:Single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) are genetic variations that influence lactase expression and persistence."}{"title": "HIPOLACTASIA DEL ADULTO:Hipolactasia del adulto es la causa m\u00e1s frecuente de intolerancia a los hidratos de carbono, t\u00edpica en ni\u00f1os mayores y adultos."}{"title": "PERIODO PERINATAL:El per\u00edodo perinatal es el tiempo alrededor del nacimiento, donde la expresi\u00f3n de lactasa aumenta."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE INTESTINO IRRITABLE:The \"S\u00edndrome de Intestino Irritable\" (Irritable Bowel Syndrome, IBS) is a common gastrointestinal disorder characterized by a range of symptoms including cramping, abdominal pain, bloating, gas, and alterations in bowel habits such as diarrhea or constipation. It is classified as a functional gastrointestinal disorder, meaning that it affects the normal functioning of the digestive system without any identifiable structural abnormalities. Symptoms often worsen after meals and can include abdominal pain and urgency to defecate.\n\nDiagnosis of IBS requires differentiation from other conditions, such as lactose intolerance and celiac disease, as it can exhibit similar symptoms. Additionally, IBS can be influenced by food intolerances and may exacerbate symptoms related to fructose malabsorption. Current research is exploring potential treatments for IBS, including the use of probiotics, to help manage its symptoms effectively."}{"title": "POLIMORFISMOS DE NUCLE\u00d3TIDO \u00daNICO:Los polimorfismos de nucle\u00f3tido \u00fanico son variaciones gen\u00e9ticas que afectan la expresi\u00f3n del gen LCT y la persistencia de lactasa."}{"title": "INTOLERANCIA A LACTOSA:Lactose intolerance is a condition known as \"INTOLERANCIA A LACTOSA,\" where individuals are unable to properly digest lactose, a sugar found in milk and dairy products. This condition can also manifest as a secondary issue for patients who have celiac disease, indicating a potential link between the two conditions."}{"title": "FINLAND:Finland is a country where the majority of patients with congenital lactase deficiency have been described."}{"title": "LACTOSE INTOLERANCE:Lactose Intolerance is a common condition affecting approximately 10% of the population, characterized by the inability to digest lactose, a sugar found in milk. This condition arises from a deficiency in the enzyme responsible for breaking down lactose, leading to various gastrointestinal symptoms after the consumption of dairy products. Individuals with lactose intolerance often experience discomfort and digestive issues, which can also impact their calcium intake from dairy sources. Overall, lactose intolerance presents significant challenges for those affected, particularly in managing their diet and ensuring adequate nutrition."}{"title": "LACTASE DEFICIENCY:Lactase deficiency refers to the reduced activity of the lactase enzyme, which can lead to lactose intolerance."}{"title": "CELIAC DISEASE:Celiac disease is an autoimmune disorder triggered by the ingestion of gluten, which leads to damage in the small intestine. This damage can result in malabsorption of essential nutrients, including calcium, thereby impacting bone health and potentially leading to various nutritional deficiencies. Additionally, the condition can cause secondary lactose intolerance due to the impairment of the intestinal lining. Celiac disease manifests through a range of gastrointestinal and extraintestinal symptoms, necessitating a strict gluten-free diet to manage the disorder and prevent further complications."}{"title": "ABDOMINAL PAIN:Abdominal pain is a symptom that can arise from lactose intolerance due to the inability to digest lactose properly."}{"title": "METEORISM:Meteorism, or bloating, is a symptom that can occur in individuals with lactose intolerance after consuming lactose."}{"title": "LACTOSE ELIMINATION DIET:A lactose elimination diet is a method used to diagnose lactose intolerance by removing lactose from the diet and observing symptom resolution."}{"title": "HYDROGEN BREATH TEST:The hydrogen breath test is a non-invasive diagnostic procedure utilized to assess lactose intolerance. This test measures hydrogen levels in the breath following the ingestion of lactose. By analyzing the hydrogen concentration, healthcare providers can determine whether an individual has difficulty digesting lactose, thereby diagnosing lactose intolerance effectively."}{"title": "DIARRHEA:Diarrhea is a common condition that can arise in various medical contexts. It frequently occurs as a complication in patients undergoing antineoplastic treatment, necessitating dietary adjustments and careful management to mitigate its effects. Additionally, diarrhea is a prevalent symptom associated with celiac disease, typically triggered by the consumption of gluten. This highlights the importance of understanding the underlying causes of diarrhea in different patient populations to provide appropriate care and dietary guidance."}{"title": "ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY:The measurement of enzymatic activity is crucial for diagnosing lactose intolerance, particularly through biopsies."}{"title": "GENETIC STUDY:Genetic studies are conducted to identify mutations in the LCT gene associated with lactose intolerance."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL OBJECTIVES:Nutritional objectives are designed to prevent severe complications associated with hereditary hemochromatosis through specific dietary recommendations and management strategies. Additionally, these objectives emphasize the importance of managing lactose intake to alleviate symptoms while ensuring that individuals receive adequate nutrition. Furthermore, they focus on reducing the intake of fructose and sorbitol to help alleviate symptoms in individuals with dietary intolerances. Overall, the nutritional objectives encompass a comprehensive approach to dietary management aimed at improving health outcomes for individuals with various dietary needs and conditions."}{"title": "CALCIUM AND VITAMIN D:Calcium and Vitamin D supplements are recommended for individuals with lactose intolerance to prevent bone density loss."}{"title": "BIOPSY:A biopsy is a medical procedure used to diagnose lactose intolerance by examining intestinal tissue for enzymatic activity."}{"title": "DIET WITHOUT LACTOSE:A diet without lactose is recommended for individuals with lactose intolerance to avoid symptoms and maintain nutritional balance."}{"title": "PREMATURE INFANTS:Premature infants may require lactose-free formulas due to their inability to digest lactose effectively."}{"title": "LACTASE:Lactase is the enzyme responsible for breaking down lactose, and its deficiency leads to lactose intolerance."}{"title": "SUERO L\u00c1CTEO:Suero l\u00e1cteo is whey, a byproduct of cheese production that contains lactose."}{"title": "LACTASAS:Lactasas are commercial preparations that can be added to foods to help increase tolerance to lactose."}{"title": "DISAC\u00c1RIDAS:Disac\u00e1ridas refer to the category of sugars that includes lactose, which can cause intolerance symptoms if not digested properly."}{"title": "CHOCOLATE:Chocolate is a food product that can contain lactose, particularly in milk chocolate varieties. It is also recognized for its magnesium content, although consumption should be moderated due to its potential health implications. Additionally, chocolate has a high phosphorus/protein ratio, which makes it discouraged for renal patients. Notably, dark chocolate is highlighted for its flavonoid content and is associated with potential health benefits related to heart health."}{"title": "CEREALES DE DESAYUNO:CEREALES DE DESAYUNO, or breakfast cereals, encompass a wide variety of products that can differ significantly in their ingredients and nutritional content. These cereals may vary in gluten content, with some options being suitable for gluten-free diets, catering to individuals with gluten sensitivities or celiac disease. Additionally, CEREALES DE DESAYUNO may contain lactose as an ingredient, which is important for those who are lactose intolerant to consider when selecting their breakfast options. Overall, CEREALES DE DESAYUNO offers diverse choices that can accommodate different dietary needs and preferences."}{"title": "PAN INDUSTRIAL:Pan industrial refers to industrially produced bread, which can sometimes contain lactose."}{"title": "BIZCOCHOS:Bizcochos are baked goods that may include lactose in their ingredients."}{"title": "DULCES:DULCES refers to sweets and candies, which may contain lactose. These treats are typically enjoyed for their delightful flavors and textures. However, dietary guidelines suggest that DULCES should be consumed occasionally and in moderation to maintain a balanced diet."}{"title": "SALSA:Salsa refers to sauces that may contain lactose as part of their composition."}{"title": "EMBUTIDOS:EMBUTIDOS are processed meats that are generally advised to be limited in children's diets due to various health concerns. These meats can sometimes contain lactose and may also include gluten, which necessitates caution for individuals with celiac disease, depending on the manufacturer's information. EMBUTIDOS typically have a high sodium content and are discouraged in diets that require gluten control, as they may contain gluten. Nutritionally, they provide 2.4 mg of iron per 100 grams, but their high fat content raises concerns, despite having an acceptable phosphorus ratio. Overall, dietary guidelines recommend that processed meats like EMBUTIDOS should be consumed occasionally and in moderation, and they are not permitted in modified diets."}{"title": "CARAMELOS:Caramelos are sweet confections that are enjoyed as snacks and can come in various forms, including candies and gummies. These candies may include lactose in their ingredients and often contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol, which can contribute to dietary intolerances. Additionally, it is important to note that caramelos and gummies may contain gluten, so individuals with celiac disease should verify the ingredients before consumption."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS ENLATADOS:Productos enlatados refers to canned products, which may contain lactose."}{"title": "ALIMENTO:Alimento refers to food products, encompassing a wide range of items that vary in sodium content, including both processed and fresh foods. These food products are often subject to thermal treatment to ensure their safety and quality."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT CONG\u00c9NITO:Congenital deficit is a hereditary autosomal recessive disease with very low prevalence, affecting 5-10% of the population in Greenland and Canada, caused by a mutation in the SI gene, leading to symptoms upon the introduction of sucrose in the diet."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT SECUNDARIO:Secondary deficit occurs due to any intestinal pathology that reduces the activity of disaccharidases, similar to secondary lactase deficiency, with enzymatic activity usually recovering when the intestinal disease is resolved."}{"title": "RECHAZO A LOS ALIMENTOS AZUCARADOS:Rejection of sugary foods is a behavioral response in children with congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase due to the associated symptoms."}{"title": "SLC5A1:SLC5A1 is the gene that encodes the SGLT1 transporter, mutations in which cause glucose-galactose malabsorption."}{"title": "MALABSORCI\u00d3N DE GLUCOSA-GALACTOSA:Glucose-galactose malabsorption is a rare autosomal recessive hereditary disease characterized by severe diarrhea and dehydration upon lactose introduction in infants."}{"title": "HECES \u00c1CIDAS:Acidic stools are a clinical manifestation associated with glucose-galactose malabsorption, indicating malabsorption issues."}{"title": "DESHIDRATACI\u00d3N HIPEROSMOLAR:Hyperosmolar dehydration is a serious condition that can occur in infants suffering from glucose-galactose malabsorption due to severe diarrhea."}{"title": "TEST DE HIDR\u00d3GENO ESPIRADO:The \"TEST DE HIDR\u00d3GENO ESPIRADO\" is a diagnostic method utilized to assess various gastrointestinal conditions. Primarily, it is employed to diagnose lactose intolerance by measuring the amount of hydrogen present in the breath following the ingestion of lactose. Additionally, the test serves as a tool to confirm glucose-galactose malabsorption by evaluating hydrogen levels after the consumption of sugar. This dual application highlights the test's significance in identifying different types of carbohydrate malabsorption issues."}{"title": "SUSTRATOS:Substrates refer to the sugars that are restricted or eliminated from the diet of patients with glucose-galactose malabsorption."}{"title": "MALABSORCI\u00d3N DE FRUCTOSA:Malabsorci\u00f3n de fructosa is a condition characterized by the inability to absorb fructose properly, leading to gastrointestinal symptoms such as flatulence, diarrhea, and abdominal pain."}{"title": "FORMULAS COMERCIALES:Formulas comerciales are special dietary formulas used for individuals with fructosa malabsorption, often containing fructosa or are free of carbohydrates."}{"title": "FLATULENCIA:Flatulencia is another gastrointestinal symptom that can occur due to malabsorci\u00f3n de fructosa, leading to discomfort."}{"title": "POL\u00cdMEROS DE GLUCOSA:Pol\u00edmeros de glucosa are complex carbohydrates that consist of glucose polymers. They are particularly relevant in dietary considerations for individuals with specific metabolic conditions. For those with fructosa malabsorption, it is advised to avoid these polymers due to potential adverse effects. Conversely, in certain dietary treatments, particularly in special situations, pol\u00edmeros de glucosa are added to liquids to enhance energy intake. Additionally, they play a crucial role in the dietary management of patients with Maple Syrup Urine Disease, where they are utilized to prevent catabolism. Thus, while they can be beneficial in specific contexts, caution is warranted for individuals with certain metabolic disorders."}{"title": "REHIDRATACI\u00d3N:Rehidrataci\u00f3n refers to the process of restoring fluids, which is crucial for individuals experiencing diarrhea due to malabsorci\u00f3n de fructosa."}{"title": "SII:SII, or Irritable Bowel Syndrome, is a common functional gastrointestinal disorder that affects the large intestine. It is characterized by a range of symptoms including cramping, abdominal pain, bloating, gas, and alterations in bowel habits such as diarrhea or constipation. The condition can be influenced by the intake of certain carbohydrates, particularly fructans, fructose, and sorbitol, which may trigger or exacerbate symptoms. Effective management of SII often requires careful dietary adjustments to minimize discomfort and maintain digestive health."}{"title": "ALIMENTARY PRODUCTS:Alimentary products refer to food items that may contain varying levels of fructose and sorbitol, impacting dietary intolerances."}{"title": "LIGHT PRODUCTS:Light products are food items marketed as low-calorie, which may contain high levels of fructose and sorbitol."}{"title": "DIABETIC PRODUCTS:Diabetic products are specially formulated foods that may still contain fructose and sorbitol, impacting those with intolerances."}{"title": "FRUIT JUICES:Fruit juices often contain high levels of fructose and can exacerbate symptoms in individuals with dietary intolerances."}{"title": "PATIENTS WITH INTESTINAL DISEASE:Patients with intestinal diseases may require dietary adjustments to manage symptoms related to fructose and sorbitol intake."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FRUCTANOS:Foods high in fructans include wheat and certain vegetables, which can lead to digestive issues for some individuals."}{"title": "FODMAP:FODMAP refers to a group of short-chain carbohydrates that are poorly absorbed in the small intestine and can lead to digestive issues in some individuals, particularly those with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) and Crohn's disease. These fermentable carbohydrates can trigger gastrointestinal symptoms, making them a significant focus of dietary recommendations for individuals sensitive to them. The study of FODMAPs is also relevant in the context of gluten sensitivity, as they can exacerbate symptoms in susceptible individuals."}{"title": "SENSIBILIDAD VISCERAL:Visceral sensitivity refers to the heightened response of individuals to gastrointestinal stimuli, which may contribute to symptoms of intolerance."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS PROCESADOS:ALIMENTOS PROCESADOS, or processed foods, are often characterized by their high phosphorus content, primarily due to the additives used in their production. As a result, these foods should be limited in renal diets to promote better health outcomes for individuals with kidney issues."}{"title": "RA\u00cdZ DE ACHICORIA:Ra\u00edz de achicoria is a food item that is high in fructans and can contribute to FODMAP-related digestive symptoms."}{"title": "CENTENO:Centeno, also known as rye, is a cereal grain that contains gluten, making it unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. It can also contain fructans, which may contribute to digestive issues related to FODMAPs. As such, those with gluten sensitivities or FODMAP-related digestive concerns should avoid consuming centeno."}{"title": "CEBOLLINO:Cebollino is a food item that contains fructans and can affect those with FODMAP intolerance."}{"title": "AVENA:Avena, commonly known as oats, is a cereal grain that is generally considered to have a low FODMAP content, making it suitable for many individuals with dietary sensitivities. It is low in purines, which can be beneficial for those managing uric acid levels. However, there are some concerns regarding its safety for patients with celiac disease. While oats can be consumed by individuals with celiac disease if they are processed to avoid gluten contamination, there remains some uncertainty about their potential toxicity for these patients. Additionally, while oats can be included in gluten-free diets, they may still pose issues for those with gluten sensitivity. Overall, Avena is a versatile grain that can be beneficial for many, but caution is advised for individuals with specific dietary restrictions."}{"title": "AJO:AJO, commonly known as garlic, is recognized for its numerous health benefits. It is particularly noted for its anti-aggregating properties, which can help prevent the clumping of platelets in the blood, thereby promoting cardiovascular health. Additionally, garlic has a positive influence on lipid metabolism, contributing to better management of cholesterol levels. Overall, AJO is valued not only as a flavorful ingredient in various cuisines but also for its potential health-promoting effects."}{"title": "NUTRICIONISTA:A nutritionist is a professional who specializes in the study of nutrition and dietary practices, providing guidance on dietary restrictions and nutritional support for patients with specific health conditions."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FODMAP:Foods high in FODMAPs include certain dairy products, fruits, vegetables, and grains that can lead to gastrointestinal discomfort for sensitive individuals."}{"title": "ALTERNATIVAS:Alternatives to high FODMAP foods are suggested to ensure a nutritionally adequate diet while avoiding foods that may cause symptoms."}{"title": "BLOQUE HIDRATOS DE CARBONO:A section discussing carbohydrates and their digestion mechanisms, including genetic and molecular aspects."}{"title": "SWALLOW DM:Swallow DM is an author of a study on intolerance to lactose and other dietary sugars published in Drug Metabolism and Disposition."}{"title": "LEVIN RJ:Levin RJ is an author who wrote about the digestion and absorption of carbohydrates in the American Journal of Clinical Nutrition."}{"title": "ROJAS HIDALGO E:Rojas Hidalgo E is an author discussing disorders of carbohydrate digestion and metabolism in his book on carbohydrates in human nutrition."}{"title": "MORANGELA M:Morangela M is an author who studied the effects of potassium citrate supplementation on bone metabolism."}{"title": "ALI M:Ali M is an author who wrote about hereditary fructose intolerance in a medical genetics journal."}{"title": "CORNEJO VE:Cornejo VE is an author discussing alterations in fructose metabolism in a Chilean nutrition review."}{"title": "TREEM WR:Treem WR is an author who wrote about congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency in a pediatric gastroenterology journal."}{"title": "ROMAGNUOLE J:Romagnuole J is an author recognized for contributions to the field of gastroenterology, specifically focusing on the use of breath tests. They have participated in a study that examines the application of breath tests within gastroenterology practices and have also conducted a review of these tests, highlighting their relevance and utility in clinical settings."}{"title": "OLIGOSAC\u00c1RIDOS:Oligosaccharides are carbohydrates that can cause digestive issues for some people, often discussed in the context of dietary restrictions."}{"title": "SORBITE:Sorbitol is a sugar alcohol used as a sweetener that can cause digestive issues for some people."}{"title": "ARROZ:ARROZ, commonly known as rice, is a cereal that is safe for patients with celiac disease, as it does not contain gluten. It is recognized as a staple food and is often recommended for individuals with gluten intolerance. Additionally, rice is permitted in modified diets and is categorized as part of the cereal group, making it a versatile and essential component of many dietary plans."}{"title": "MA\u00cdZ:MA\u00cdZ, commonly known as corn, is a gluten-free cereal grain that is safe for individuals with celiac disease. It is widely used in various food products due to its gluten-free properties. In Spanish, it is also referred to as \"el ma\u00edz,\" emphasizing that it is a cereal that does not contain gluten, making it a suitable option for patients with celiac disease."}{"title": "MIJO:Millet is a gluten-free grain that is often included in diets for those with gluten intolerance."}{"title": "POLENTA:Polenta is a dish made from cornmeal that is gluten-free and suitable for those with gluten sensitivity."}{"title": "QUINOA:Quinoa is a gluten-free grain that is highly regarded for its nutritional benefits, particularly its high protein content. It is commonly used in products specifically designed for individuals with celiac disease, making it a popular choice for gluten-free diets."}{"title": "SORGO:SORGO, also known as sorghum, is a gluten-free cereal that is safe for individuals with celiac disease and those with gluten intolerance. It can be utilized in a variety of food products, making it a versatile option for those seeking gluten-free alternatives in their diet."}{"title": "PASTELES:PASTELES are baked goods that typically contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. However, it is important to note that cakes can vary in their gluten content, and some may be specifically made to accommodate gluten-free diets. This means that while many traditional pasteles are harmful to those with gluten sensitivities, there are also options available that cater to gluten-free needs."}{"title": "CAF\u00c9:CAF\u00c9 refers to coffee, a popular beverage enjoyed by many individuals. It is gluten-free and has no established guidelines for consumption by children. Coffee is included in modified diets as part of the beverage group. Additionally, it is noted that coffee can have a variable effect on cardiovascular risk, with moderate consumption associated with a lower risk. Furthermore, coffee is mentioned in the context of a strict low-sodium diet."}{"title": "GIN:Gin is a distilled alcoholic beverage that is typically gluten-free."}{"title": "CERVEZA:Beer is an alcoholic beverage that is often made from gluten-containing grains, but gluten-free options are available."}{"title": "VINO SECO:Dry wine is an alcoholic beverage that is gluten-free and often enjoyed by individuals with gluten intolerance."}{"title": "VODKA:Vodka is a distilled alcoholic beverage that is typically gluten-free."}{"title": "WHISKY:Whiskey is a distilled alcoholic beverage that is typically gluten-free."}{"title": "T\u00c9:T\u00c9 is a beverage that has been the subject of various studies, particularly concerning its relationship with cardiovascular risk, which shows non-linear effects based on the quantity consumed. Additionally, T\u00c9 contains oxalate, a compound that may increase the risk of developing kidney stones. Despite these concerns, T\u00c9 is gluten-free, making it a suitable option for many individuals. Furthermore, T\u00c9 is included in the list of permitted beverages for modified diets, highlighting its versatility and acceptance in various dietary contexts."}{"title": "SCHILLER D:Schiller D is an author who collaborated on a review regarding the use of breath tests in gastroenterology."}{"title": "BAILEY RJ:Bailey RJ is an author involved in the evidence-based review of breath tests in gastroenterology."}{"title": "RASINPER\u00c4 H:Rasinper\u00e4 H is an author who researched genetic tests for diagnosing adult-type hypolactasia in children."}{"title": "SAVILAHTI E:Savilahti E is an author who contributed to the study on diagnosing adult-type hypolactasia."}{"title": "ENATTAH NS:Enattah NS is an author involved in the research on genetic testing for lactose intolerance."}{"title": "KOUKKANEN M:Koukkanen M is an author who participated in the study on diagnosing lactose intolerance."}{"title": "T\u00d6TTERMAN N:T\u00f6tterman N is an author who contributed to the research on adult-type hypolactasia."}{"title": "LINDAHL L:Lindahl L is an author involved in the study regarding genetic tests for lactose intolerance."}{"title": "CHOI YK:Choi YK is an author who wrote about fructose intolerance in gastroenterology."}{"title": "JOHLIN FC JR:Johlin FC Jr is an author who contributed to the research on fructose intolerance."}{"title": "SUMMERS RW:Summers RW is an author involved in the study of fructose intolerance."}{"title": "JACKSON M:Jackson M is an author who participated in the research on fructose absorption."}{"title": "RAO SS:Rao SS is an author who evaluated the ability of the human intestine to absorb fructose."}{"title": "SKOOG SM:Skoog SM is an author who reviewed dietary fructose and gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "CLAYTON B:Clayton B is an author who discussed dietetic treatment of inherited metabolic disease."}{"title": "GREEN A:Green A is an author who contributed to the discussion on dietetic treatment of metabolic diseases."}{"title": "MACDONALD A:MacDonald A is an author involved in the treatment of inherited metabolic diseases."}{"title": "RUIZ PONS M:Ruiz Pons M is an author who approached nutritional treatment for metabolic errors."}{"title": "SANTANA VEGA C:Santana Vega C is an author who contributed to the study on nutritional treatment of metabolic disorders."}{"title": "TRUJILLO ARMAS R:Trujillo Armas R is an author involved in the research on nutritional treatment for metabolic errors."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ-VALVERDE F:S\u00e1nchez-Valverde F is an author who contributed to the study on metabolic disorders."}{"title": "CRIGLER JF:Crigler JF is an author involved in the study of cornstarch regimens for metabolic disease treatment."}{"title": "VELASCO FUENTES N:Velasco Fuentes N is an author who discussed restricted galactose diets."}{"title": "CAMPANO BASCU\u00d1AN M:Campano Bascu\u00f1an M is an author who contributed to the study on restricted galactose diets."}{"title": "SHILS ME:Shils ME is an author who wrote about lactose-controlled diets."}{"title": "OLSON JA:Olson JA is an author involved in the research on nutrition in health and disease."}{"title": "SHINE M:Shine M is an author who contributed to the study on lactose-controlled diets."}{"title": "ROSS AC:Ross AC is an author who discussed the role of lactose in nutrition."}{"title": "LOVELACE HY:Lovelace HY is an author who researched lactose intolerance and calcium intake."}{"title": "BARR SI:Barr SI is an author involved in the study of lactose intolerance symptoms."}{"title": "DI STEFANO M:Di Stefano M is an author who researched lactose malabsorption and peak bone mass."}{"title": "VENETO G:Veneto G is an author who contributed to the study on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "MALSERVISI S:Malservisi S is an author involved in the research on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "CECHETTI L:Cechetti L is an author who participated in the study on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "MINGUZZI L:Minguzzi L is an author involved in the research on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "STROCCHI A:Strocchi A is an author who contributed to the study on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "SANTANA VEGA C<|(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "TURK D:"}{"title": "LEREBOURS E:Lerebours E is an author who researched the effects of yogurt and fermented milk on lactose absorption."}{"title": "N'DJITOYAP NDAM C:N'Djitoyap Ndam C is an author who has made significant contributions to the study of yogurt and its effects on lactose absorption. Through their research, N'Djitoyap Ndam C has explored how yogurt can influence the body's ability to absorb lactose, providing valuable insights into dietary practices and health."}{"title": "LAVOINE A:Lavoine A is an author who is actively involved in research concerning yogurt and lactose absorption. This research focuses on the effects of yogurt on lactose absorption, highlighting Lavoine A's contributions to the field."}{"title": "HELLOT MF:Hellot MF is an author who has conducted research on the effects of yogurt in relation to lactase activity and lactose absorption, particularly focusing on individuals who are lactase-deficient. Through their studies, Hellot MF has explored how yogurt consumption may influence the ability to digest lactose, providing insights into dietary management for those with lactose intolerance."}{"title": "ANTOINE JM:Antoine JM is an author who has contributed to research focused on yogurt and lactose absorption. His work in this area highlights the significance of yogurt in relation to lactose digestion and its potential benefits for individuals with lactose intolerance."}{"title": "COLIN R:Colin R is an author known for his contributions to the study of yogurt and its effects on lactose absorption. He has specifically researched how yogurt impacts lactose absorption in individuals who are lactase-deficient, highlighting the potential benefits of yogurt for those with lactose intolerance."}{"title": "JOHN HOPKINS UNIVERSITY:John Hopkins University is a research university located in Baltimore, known for its contributions to various fields including medicine and nutrition."}{"title": "GARCIA-PERIS P:Garcia-Peris P is an author who contributed to the recommendations on nutrition for lactose intolerance."}{"title": "TERRY G. J. DERKS:Terry G. J. Derks is an author who has researched lipids in hepatic glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ AUGUST\u00cdN:Mart\u00ednez August\u00edn is an author who has worked on carbohydrate metabolism in nutrition."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE TYPE III:Glycogen storage disease type III is a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to store and use glycogen."}{"title": "POCHART P:Pochart P is an author who studied the effects of viable starter cultures on lactose absorption."}{"title": "DEWIT O:Dewit O is an author who contributed to the research on yogurt ingestion in lactase-deficient humans."}{"title": "DESJEUX JF:Desjeux JF is an author involved in the study of lactose absorption after yogurt ingestion."}{"title": "BOURLIOUX P:Bourlioux P is an author who has researched the effects of yogurt on lactose absorption."}{"title": "SAVAIANO DA:Savaiano DA is an author who studied lactose malabsorption from various dairy products in lactase-deficient individuals."}{"title": "ABOUELANOUAR A:AbouElAnouar A is an author who contributed to the research on lactose malabsorption."}{"title": "SMITH DE:Smith DE is an author who has researched lactose malabsorption in lactase-deficient individuals."}{"title": "LEVITT MD:Levitt MD is an author who studied lactose malabsorption from yogurt and other dairy products."}{"title": "HICKEY MW:Hickey MW is an author who researched the transport and metabolism of lactose in lactobacilli."}{"title": "HILLIER AJ:Hillier AJ is an author involved in the study of lactose transport in homofermentative lactobacilli."}{"title": "JAGO GR:Jago GR is an author who contributed to the research on lactose metabolism."}{"title": "FOUCAUD C:Foucaud C is an author who studied the lactose transport system of Streptococcus thermophilus."}{"title": "POOLMAN B:Poolman B is an author involved in the research of lactose transport systems in bacteria."}{"title": "HUIDEKOPER HH:Huidekoper HH is an author who studied glucose homeostasis in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "VISSER G:Visser G is an author who contributed to the research on glucose production in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "ACKERMANS MT:Ackermans MT is an author involved in the study of glucose homeostasis in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "SAUERWEIN HP:Sauerwein HP is an author who researched glucose production in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "WIJBURG FA:Wijburg FA is an author who studied endogenous glucose production in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "SENTNER PC:Sentner PC is an author who researched glycogen storage disease type III and its management."}{"title": "HOOGEVEEN IJ:Hoogeveen IJ is an author involved in the study of dietary interventions in glycogen storage disease."}{"title": "WEINSTEIN DA:Weinstein DA is an author who studied glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "SANTER R:Santer R is an author who contributed to the research on glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "MCKIERNAN PJ:McKiernan PJ is an author involved in the study of glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "BRAMBILLA A:Brambilla A is an author who researched dietary management in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "MANNARINO S:Mannarino S is an author who studied cardiomyopathy in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "PRETESE R:Pretes R is an author involved in research on glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "GASPERINI S:Gasperini S is an author who studied dietary interventions in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "GALIMBERTI C:Galimberti C is an author who researched cardiomyopathy in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "PARINI R:Parini R is an author involved in the study of glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "VALAYANNOPOULOS V:Valayannopoulos V is an author who studied treatment options for glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "BAJOLLE F:Bajolle F is an author who contributed to research on glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "ARNOUX JB:Arnoux JB is an author involved in the study of glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "DUBOIS S:Dubois S is an author who studied treatment for glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "SANNIER N:Sannier N is an author involved in research on glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "BAUSSAN C:Baussan C is an author who studied treatment options for glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "D,L-3-HYDROXYBUTYRATE:D,L-3-Hydroxybutyrate is a compound studied for its potential treatment effects in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "KETOGENIC DIET:The ketogenic diet is a high-fat, low-carbohydrate dietary approach that has been utilized in the management of various health conditions, particularly certain metabolic disorders and intractable seizure disorders. It has been studied for its effects on glycogen storage disease type III and is primarily recognized for its efficacy in treating epilepsy, especially in children and adults with intractable seizures. The diet has shown significant effectiveness in seizure control and the management of various neurological disorders, making it a valuable intervention in both clinical and research settings."}{"title": "HIGH-PROTEIN DIET:A high-protein diet is a dietary intervention that is often recommended for individuals with certain metabolic disorders, including glycogen storage disease type III. This type of diet is designed to help manage symptoms associated with these disorders while providing adequate nutrition. The focus on increased protein intake can play a crucial role in supporting metabolic health and addressing specific dietary needs related to these conditions."}{"title": "VALAYANNOPOULOS:Valayannopoulos is a researcher involved in the treatment of severe cardiomyopathy in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "BAJOLLE:Bajolle is a researcher who co-authored a study on cardiomyopathy treatment in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "ARNOUX:Arnoux is a researcher who contributed to the study on cardiomyopathy treatment in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "DUBOIS:Dubois is a researcher involved in the treatment of severe cardiomyopathy in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "SANNIER:Sannier is a researcher who co-authored a study on cardiomyopathy treatment in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "BAUSSAN:Baussan is a researcher involved in the treatment of severe cardiomyopathy in glycogen storage disease type III."}{"title": "GROSS:Gross is a researcher who studied the implications of fruits and vegetables as a source of galactose in patients with galactosaemia."}{"title": "ACOSTA:Acosta is a researcher who co-authored a study on dietary implications for patients with galactosaemia."}{"title": "PUNTIS:Puntis is a researcher who addressed diagnostic challenges in congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "ZAMVAR:Zamvar is a researcher who co-authored a study on congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "LUCKE:L\u00fccke is a researcher who studied the effects of sacroidase therapy in sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "KEISER:Keiser is a researcher involved in the study of sucrase-isomaltase deficiency in infancy."}{"title": "ILLSINGER:Illsinger is a researcher who contributed to the study on sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "NAIM:Naim is a researcher engaged in the study of both congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency and lactose intolerance. This dual focus highlights Naim's expertise in the field of carbohydrate malabsorption disorders, contributing valuable insights into these conditions."}{"title": "DAS:Das is a researcher who studied the effects of sacroidase therapy in sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "ROBAYO-TORRES:Robayo-Torres is a researcher who studied 13C-breath tests for sucrose digestion in patients."}{"title": "OPEKUN:Opekun is a researcher who co-authored a study on sucrose digestion in congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "QUEZADA-CALVILLO:Quezada-Calvillo is a researcher involved in the study of sucrose digestion."}{"title": "VILLA:Villa is a researcher who contributed to the study on sucrose digestion in patients."}{"title": "NAVARRETE:Navarrete is a researcher involved in the study of sucrose digestion."}{"title": "WILDER-SMITH:Wilder-Smith is a researcher who studied fructose transporters in patients with fructose intolerance."}{"title": "LI:Li is a researcher involved in the study of fructose transporters in patients."}{"title": "HO:Ho is a researcher who contributed to the study on fructose transporters."}{"title": "LEONG:Leong is a researcher involved in the study of fructose transporters."}{"title": "WONG:Wong is a researcher who studied fructose transporters in patients."}{"title": "JOAY:Joay is a researcher involved in the study of fructose transporters."}{"title": "FERRARIS:Ferraris is a researcher who studied fructose transporters in patients."}{"title": "FEDEWA:Fedewa is a researcher who studied dietary fructose intolerance and FODMAPs."}{"title": "RAO:Rao is a researcher who co-authored a study on dietary fructose intolerance."}{"title": "QUINLIVAN:Quinlivan is a researcher who studied pharmacological treatment for McArdle's disease."}{"title": "BEYNON:Beynon is a researcher who co-authored a study on McArdle's disease treatment."}{"title": "MARTINUZZI:Martinuzzi is a researcher involved in the study of McArdle's disease treatment."}{"title": "AMIRI:Amiri is a researcher who studied lactose intolerance and its linkage to cancers."}{"title": "DIEKMANN:Diekmann is a researcher involved in the study of lactose intolerance."}{"title": "VON K\u00d6CKRITZ-BLICKWEDE:Von K\u00f6ckritz-Blickwede is a researcher who studied lactose intolerance."}{"title": "SUAREZ:Suarez is a researcher who studied symptoms of lactose intolerance."}{"title": "SAVAIANO:Savaiano is a researcher who studied lactose digestion from yogurt."}{"title": "ENATTAH:Enattah is a researcher who studied lactase persistence in humans."}{"title": "TRUDEAU:Trudeau is a researcher involved in the study of lactase persistence."}{"title": "PIMENOFF:Pimenoff is a researcher who studied lactase persistence."}{"title": "MAIURI:Maiuri is a researcher involved in the study of lactase persistence."}{"title": "AURICCHIO:Auricchio is a researcher who studied lactase persistence."}{"title": "GRECO:Greco is a researcher involved in the study of lactase persistence."}{"title": "OLDS:Olds is a researcher who studied lactase persistence DNA variant."}{"title": "SIBLEY:Sibley is a researcher involved in the study of lactase promoter activity."}{"title": "BERSAGLIERI:Bersaglieri is a researcher who studied genetic signatures of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "SABETI:Sabeti is a researcher involved in the study of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "PATTERSON:Patterson is a researcher who studied genetic signatures of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "VANDERPLOEG:Vanderploeg is a researcher involved in the study of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "SCHAFFNER:Schaffner is a researcher who studied genetic signatures of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "DRAKE:Drake is a researcher involved in the study of lactase gene selection."}{"title": "LEWINSKY:Lewinsky is a researcher who studied T-13910 DNA variant associated with lactase persistence."}{"title": "JENSEN:Jensen is a researcher involved in the study of lactase persistence."}{"title": "MOLLER:Moller is a researcher who studied lactase persistence."}{"title": "STENSBALLE:Stensballe is a researcher involved in the study of lactase persistence."}{"title": "OLSEN:Olsen is a researcher who studied lactase persistence."}{"title": "TROELSEN:Troelsen is a researcher(\"entity\""}{"title": "GALACTOSAEMIA:Galactosaemia is a genetic disorder that affects the body's ability to process galactose, requiring dietary management."}{"title": "CONGENITAL SUCRASE-ISOMALTASE DEFICIENCY:Congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency is a genetic disorder that impairs the digestion of sucrose and maltose, leading to gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "MCCARDLE'S DISEASE:McArdle's disease is a glycogen storage disease characterized by an inability to break down glycogen in muscles, leading to exercise intolerance."}{"title": "LACTASE PERSISTENCE:Lactase persistence refers to the continued production of lactase enzyme into adulthood, allowing for the digestion of lactose."}{"title": "FODMAPS:FODMAPs are a group of fermentable oligosaccharides, disaccharides, monosaccharides, and polyols, which are short-chain carbohydrates that can lead to digestive issues in certain individuals. This is particularly true for those suffering from irritable bowel syndrome (IBS)."}{"title": "SUCRASE-ISOMALTASE THERAPY:Sucrase-isomaltase therapy is a treatment approach for individuals with congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency, involving enzyme replacement."}{"title": "13C-BREATH TEST:The 13C-breath test is a diagnostic tool used to assess carbohydrate digestion, particularly in conditions like congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "ENZYME REPLACEMENT THERAPY:Enzyme replacement therapy is a treatment for certain genetic disorders, including congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency, to provide the missing enzyme."}{"title": "GENETIC SIGNATURES:Genetic signatures refer to specific genetic markers that can indicate the presence of certain traits or conditions, such as lactase persistence."}{"title": "DNA VARIANT:A DNA variant is a change in the DNA sequence that can affect an individual's traits, including lactase persistence."}{"title": "FUNCTIONAL ROLE:Functional role refers to the biological activity of a gene or protein, such as the role of lactase in lactose digestion."}{"title": "POSITIVE SELECTION:Positive selection refers to the evolutionary process where advantageous traits become more common in a population, such as lactase persistence in certain human populations."}{"title": "DIAGNOSTIC CHALLENGES:Diagnostic challenges refer to difficulties in accurately diagnosing conditions like congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency due to overlapping symptoms with other disorders."}{"title": "RESPONSE TO THERAPY:Response to therapy refers to how well a patient responds to a specific treatment, such as enzyme replacement therapy for congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency."}{"title": "SACROIDASE THERAPY:Sacroidase therapy is a treatment for congenital sucrase-isomaltase deficiency that involves the administration of the enzyme sacroidase to aid in carbohydrate digestion."}{"title": "FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE:Fructose intolerance is a condition where individuals have difficulty digesting fructose, leading to gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "FRUCTAN INTOLERANCE:Fructan intolerance is a condition where individuals 